Spiked controls can be used to:

1) Determine the success of the hybridization.
2) Center arrays when there is reason to think that there may be a large 
percentage of genes that express differently on different arrays
3) Used in a titration series, the spiked controls can be used to at least 
somewhat calibrate the expression levels from the array with the actual RNA 
concentration.

